1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,369
Paw Twin gives family members one shared pet record for everyday care.

2
00:00:04,569 --> 00:00:11,022
Here, two separate household accounts use fictional demonstration data to record, confirm, and hand over care.

3
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:19,783
The owner records sample weights of one point two and one point three five kilograms, seven days apart.

4
00:00:19,983 --> 00:00:26,727
The report calculates a hundred fifty gram increase, shows its sources, and keeps unrecorded intake unknown.

5
00:00:29,417 --> 00:00:34,700
The owner saves a preference candidate: Mochi likes a feather toy and rests after meals.

6
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:40,714
The other account cannot use the candidate; explicit confirmation makes it available as database memory.

7
00:00:43,417 --> 00:00:48,040
The carer opens the independent Alexa web simulator and asks what Mochi likes.

8
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:53,954
Its actual reply cites the confirmed record and shows local rules, with no live model request.

9
00:00:56,683 --> 00:01:01,767
Starting a new session clears the page conversation, while household records remain.

10
00:01:01,967 --> 00:01:07,175
The next question reads the same confirmed preference, with its source available for inspection.

11
00:01:09,883 --> 00:01:14,257
The owner asks the simulator to arrange play and checks its rule-generated draft.

12
00:01:14,457 --> 00:01:19,750
The owner selects a specific time; asking or preparing the draft does not create a task.

13
00:01:22,483 --> 00:01:26,492
Preparing the proposal preserves the draft and its current context version.

14
00:01:26,692 --> 00:01:30,606
The local check verifies that no care task exists at this stage.

15
00:01:33,283 --> 00:01:37,487
Only explicit owner confirmation creates the shared manual care task.

16
00:01:37,687 --> 00:01:42,550
The visible result says it is arranged and awaiting a person, without executing a feeder.

17
00:01:45,283 --> 00:01:49,242
The carer claims the task and records completion through the second account.

18
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:55,665
The shared activity log identifies who recorded completion, so the next family member can check the handoff.

19
00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:02,389
Back in the simulator, the carer asks what was recently completed.

20
00:02:02,589 --> 00:02:07,022
The answer names the manual care record and cites the actual completion occurrence.

21
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:13,539
The daily report now counts one completed manual care task.

22
00:02:13,739 --> 00:02:18,672
Actual intake remains unrecorded, and the report does not invent a health outcome.

23
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:26,119
After the owner deletes the preference, the carer asks again in a fresh page session.

24
00:02:26,319 --> 00:02:31,252
The next answer no longer cites that record; previous replies remain historical.

25
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:40,628
This capture uses local accounts, database memory, rule drafts, and confirmed manual tasks.

26
00:02:40,828 --> 00:02:47,736
Alexa and devices are simulated here, while the shared records, confirmations, and report calculations run locally.
